  "body": {
    "id": "prop:single-variant-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "When \\(K=1\\), \\(\\delta=0\\), \\(q_{11}=q_{21}=1\\), and \\(\\omega_1=1\\), the period-two no-prior-exposure controlled challenge risk in each arm obeys \\(b_{2a1}\\leq\\rho_{2a}(x,\\omega)\\leq b_{1a1}+b_{2a1}\\), the risk inclusion used in the proof of Theorem 1 of Janvin and Stensrud (2025).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "K",
      "delta",
      "q",
      "omega",
      "b",
      "rho",
      "x"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:reduced-history-polytope",
      "thm:exact-history-compression"
    ],
    "justification": "The no-priming endpoint \\(\\delta=0\\) checks that the expanded history construction preserves the standard one-pathogen survivor-selection geometry.",
    "gap": "This is a required calibration to Janvin and Stensrud (2025), not a claimed novelty.",
    "consumer": "Readers can verify the new program against the established one-pathogen proof boundary before using variant margins.",
    "proof_tex": "Apply the displayed constructions to their one-variant boundary specialization.  The exposure restrictions \\(q_{11}=q_{21}=1\\) and common histories imply \\(H_1^0=H_2^0=1\\) almost surely.  Write \\(R_1=R_{1a1}\\), \\(R_2^0=R^{[0]}_{2a1}\\), and \\(R_2^1=R^{[1]}_{2a1}\\).  The \\(\\delta=0\\) priming constraint is\n\\[\nP(R_1=0,R_2^1\\ne R_2^0)=0.\n\\]\nConsequently the observation map and the trial equalities yield\n\\[\nb_{1a1}=E(R_1),\n\\qquad\nb_{2a1}=E\\{R_2^1(1-R_1)\\}=E\\{R_2^0(1-R_1)\\}.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\omega_1=1\\), \\(\\rho_{2a}(x,\\omega)=E(R_2^0)\\), and hence\n\\[\n\\rho_{2a}(x,\\omega)\n=b_{2a1}+E(R_2^0R_1).\n\\]\nThe binary support gives \\(0\\leq R_2^0R_1\\leq R_1\\).  Taking expectations and using \\(E(R_1)=b_{1a1}\\) proves\n\\[\nb_{2a1}\\leq\\rho_{2a}(x,\\omega)\\leq b_{1a1}+b_{2a1}.\n\\]",
